## Human gates

Stop and ask before any change to authentication, authorisation, personal data handling, secrets or infrastructure; before anything that touches production; and before choosing or changing an AI model, prompt version or provider.
{%- endif %}
{%- if profile == 'service' %}

## Compatibility

- Public interfaces change compatibly: no renames, type changes or new required fields without a major version and a `CHANGELOG.md` entry.
- Migrations follow expand, migrate, contract.
{%- endif %}
{%- if profile == 'research' %}

## Evidence

- Nothing goes in without a registered source; record whether the primary was read.
- Absolute dates only. Delivered reports are frozen; corrections go to new records.
{%- endif %}
{%- if profile == 'site' %}

## Verification

- Run the checks against the production build, not the dev server, including the performance budget and a layout check at narrow and wide widths.
{%- endif %}
{%- if profile == 'demo' %}

## Status

This is a demo and is not maintained. Keep changes small and say so in the README.
{%- endif %}
{%- if 'multi-user' in (modules or []) %}

## Data isolation (multi-user)

- Every table that holds user data carries its scope key and is protected by the membership rule in `docs/security/authorization-matrix.md`.
- Every new table or endpoint adds rows to that matrix and a test for each row, including negative cases (another user, a former member).
{%- endif %}
{%- if 'eu-personal-data' in (modules or []) %}

## Privacy (EU personal data)

- Send third parties, models included, only the fields they need. Never log prompts, model outputs, transcripts or user content.
- New user data is private by default; any new personal data field, processor or purpose updates `docs/privacy/record-of-processing.md` and runs `privacy-check`.
{%- endif %}
{%- if 'ai-extraction' in (modules or []) %}

## AI extraction

- Model output must match `evals/schema.md`; refusals and truncated or invalid output become "needs confirmation", never saved data.
- Any change to prompts, models, the schema or validators runs the golden set (`eval` skill) and attaches the report to the PR.
{%- endif %}

